<!--
  Agent mark.

  Drawn on a 2048 viewport because the source artwork is drawn at that size.
  Android scales the drawable to the size asked of it, so this only sets the
  default; every call site sets its own size to match the icon grid the rest of
  the toolbar uses.

  Two things here are deliberate and were both wrong before:

  1. There is no android:tint on the vector, and the eyes are holes rather than
     a second colour. Compose's Icon() applies its own ColorFilter over the
     whole drawable, so any two-tone artwork collapses to one flat colour the
     moment it is tinted — the eyes were drawn in #101010 inside a #FFFFFF
     body, both got the toolbar tint, and the eyes disappeared into the
     silhouette. A hole cannot be filled by a tint, so the eyes survive on any
     background and the mark stays recolourable from the call site.

  2. The eyes are ellipses with a radius that reads at 24dp. The originals were
     72 units tall in a 2048 viewport — about 0.35dp on screen at toolbar size,
     which is sub-pixel and rendered as nothing at all. These are 176 units.
-->
